Components bundled in the Docker image
--------------------------------------

The Baycone container image bundles Debian packages that are NOT covered by the
MIT License above and remain under their own terms — most notably:

  ffmpeg / ffprobe and their libraries, which Debian builds with --enable-gpl
  (including libx264 and libx265) and distributes under the GNU General Public
  License, version 2 or later.

Baycone invokes ffmpeg and ffprobe as external processes and does not link
against them. The MIT License therefore covers Baycone's own code only; the
image as a whole is a collection of separately licensed works.

The license text of every bundled package is retained inside the image under
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.

Written offer of source code
----------------------------

All bundled Debian packages are unmodified binary packages taken from the
official Debian archive. Complete corresponding source code for the GPL-licensed
components is made publicly available by Debian at:

  https://sources.debian.org

and can be retrieved for any bundled package with:

  apt-get source <package>

For example, to obtain the source of the ffmpeg build shipped in this image, run
the following inside a container started from it:

  apt-get update && apt-get source ffmpeg

